bp3 harness - harness machinery door. Verbs:
bp3 harness supervisor <quest> [--engine muse-code|pi] [--timeout-seconds <n>] [--silence-seconds <n>] [--grace-seconds <n>]   passive loop: tell -> watch -> judge -> finalize
bp3 harness init-check [--engine muse-code|pi]   probe tape sources; blindness is W_SUPERVISOR_BLIND, never blocking
bp3 harness find-tape --run-id <id> [--entry <id>] [--before-entries <n>] [--after-entries <n>]   InitRecord-first run-id -> tape; --session-id <id> is a reverse lookup
bp3 harness watch --run-id <id> [--silence-seconds <n>] [--timeout-seconds <n>] [--grace-seconds <n>]   blocking watch: sole TERM/KILL owner
bp3 harness desk <verb> ...                      machine-local desks: derive, create, inspect, remove, prepare, check, exit, release, list
bp3 harness link mint|claim|lookup|cleanup ...   one-time link binding: mint a link, the child claims it once (E_LINK_SPENT, E_DEPTH)
bp3 harness record-init ...                      retired (E_RETIRED): use link mint/claim; the run config is the InitRecord-equivalent
bp3 harness bind-tape --run-id <id> --tape-path <p>   launcher binds a finished child's session tape (into the run config when claimed)
bp3 harness backtest [--engine muse-code|pi] [--corpus <dir>]   replay the fold over stored tapes; findings, not a gate
Aliases: s=supervisor, i=init-check, f=find-tape, w=watch, d=desk, r=record-init, t=bind-tape, b=backtest, l=link. Example: bp3 harness supervisor toy --timeout-seconds 1800
